  "text": "Design also decides what gets in. Bad data starts small. A customer entered twice. A quantity of zero. An order for a customer who isn't there. Here, each one bounces, and Postgres names the rule it broke. That rule lives in the schema, so it doesn't guard one app's front door. It guards the whole building.\n\nEven a type is a rule. In nineteen ninety-nine, NASA lost the Mars Climate Orbiter because one program wrote pound-force seconds and another read newton-seconds. The numbers were just numbers. Nothing said which. So where does a good design start? By naming the things your data is about.",
